IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa13-ch6-valuation.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 17 Chapter 6 (ss 593 to 609): public companies,
-- independent valuation of non-cash consideration. Lines 8009-8205 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- How to read an answer: see the header of coa13-ch1-shares.l4. Every name begins with the section label it implements.
-- "Six months immediately preceding" is counted with `add months` from the earlier date (a date months before another is never
-- subtracted: the library's month subtraction clamps); fork F-periods in NOTES.md.

§ `Part 17, Chapter 6: Public companies: independent valuation of non-cash consideration`

§§ `Non-cash consideration for shares (ss 593 to 597)`

-- ---- s 593: Public company: valuation of non-cash consideration for shares ------------------------------

-- src:8016 | (2) For this purpose the application of an amount standing to the credit of—
-- src:8017 | (a) any of a company's reserve accounts, or
-- src:8018 | (b) its profit and loss account,
-- src:8019 | in paying up (to any extent) shares allotted to members of the company, or premiums on shares so allotted, does not count as consideration for the allotment.
-- src:8020 | Accordingly, subsection (1) does not apply in that case.
@ref s 593(2) the application of reserves or profit and loss account in paying up shares allotted to members does not count as consideration (src:8016-8020)
GIVEN `the amount stands to the credit of a reserve account of the company or of its profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is applied in paying up (to any extent) shares allotted to members of the company, or premiums on shares so allotted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 593(2) subsection (1) applies to the allotment` MEANS
    IF `the amount stands to the credit of a reserve account of the company or of its profit and loss account` AND `it is applied in paying up (to any extent) shares allotted to members of the company, or premiums on shares so allotted`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not count as consideration for the allotment. Accordingly, subsection (1) does not apply in that case."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of reserve accounts or the profit and loss account applied in paying up shares allotted to members

-- src:8012 | (1) A public company must not allot shares as fully or partly paid up (as to their nominal value or any premium on them) otherwise than in cash unless—
-- src:8013 | (a) the consideration for the allotment has been independently valued in accordance with the provisions of this Chapter,
-- src:8014 | (b) the valuer's report has been made to the company during the six months immediately preceding the allotment of the shares, and
-- src:8015 | (c) a copy of the report has been sent to the proposed allottee.
@ref s 593(1) a public company must not allot shares otherwise than for cash unless the consideration has been independently valued, the report made within six months, and a copy sent (src:8012-8015)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up (as to their nominal value or any premium on them) otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 593(2) subsection (1) applies to the allotment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 594(1) section 593 does not apply to the allotment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 595(1) section 593 does not apply to the allotment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the consideration for the allotment has been independently valued in accordance with the provisions of Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the valuer's report was made to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date of the allotment of the shares` IS A DATE
      `a copy of the report has been sent to the proposed allottee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 593(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND `the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up (as to their nominal value or any premium on them) otherwise than in cash`
    THEN IF `s 593(2) subsection (1) applies to the allotment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Accordingly, subsection (1) does not apply in that case." (subsection (2))
         ELSE IF `s 594(1) section 593 does not apply to the allotment` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 595(1) section 593 does not apply to the allotment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section has effect subject to section 594 ... and section 595" (an exception is met)
              ELSE IF     `the consideration for the allotment has been independently valued in accordance with the provisions of Chapter 6`
                      AND `the date on which the valuer's report was made to the company` AT MOST `the date of the allotment of the shares`
                      AND `the date of the allotment of the shares` AT MOST (`add months` `the date on which the valuer's report was made to the company` 6)
                      AND `a copy of the report has been sent to the proposed allottee`
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not allot shares ... unless— (a) ... valued ..., (b) the valuer's report has been made to the company during the six months immediately preceding the allotment ..., and (c) a copy of the report has been sent to the proposed allottee" (the "unless" is met)
                   ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company must not allot shares as fully or partly paid up ... otherwise than in cash"

-- src:8021 | (3) If a company allots shares in contravention of subsection (1) and either—
-- src:8022 | (a) the allottee has not received the valuer's report required to be sent to him, or
-- src:8023 | (b) there has been some other contravention of the requirements of this section or section 596 that the allottee knew or ought to have known amounted to a contravention,
-- src:8024 | the allottee is liable to pay the company an amount equal to the aggregate of the nominal value of the shares and the whole of any premium (or, if the case so requires, so much of that aggregate as is treated as paid up by the consideration), with interest at the appropriate rate.
@ref s 593(3) the allottee is liable to pay the company where shares are allotted in contravention and the report was not received or another contravention was known (src:8021-8024)
GIVEN `the company allots shares in contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allottee has not received the valuer's report required to be sent to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been some other contravention of the requirements of section 593 or section 596 that the allottee knew or ought to have known amounted to a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 593(3) the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    IF     `the company allots shares in contravention of subsection (1)`
       AND (`the allottee has not received the valuer's report required to be sent to him` OR `there has been some other contravention of the requirements of section 593 or section 596 that the allottee knew or ought to have known amounted to a contravention`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company allots shares in contravention of subsection (1) and either (a) ... or (b) ..." (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

@ref s 593(3) the amount: the nominal value and the whole premium, or so much as is treated as paid up by the consideration (src:8024)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole of any premium on them` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up by the consideration (1 if the whole)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 593(3) the amount the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    (`the nominal value of the shares` PLUS `the whole of any premium on them`) TIMES `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up by the consideration (1 if the whole)`

-- ---- s 594: Exception to valuation requirement: arrangement with another company -----------------------

-- src:8036 | (5) In determining whether that is the case, the following shall be disregarded—
-- src:8037 | (a) shares held by or by a nominee of company A;
-- src:8038 | (b) shares held by or by a nominee of a company which is—
-- src:8039 | (i) the holding company, or a subsidiary, of company A, or
-- src:8040 | (ii) a subsidiary of such a holding company;
-- src:8041 | (c) shares held as treasury shares by company B.
@ref s 594(5) shares disregarded in deciding whether the arrangement is open to all holders of company B (src:8036-8041)
GIVEN `the shares are held by or by a nominee of company A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) company A is a subsidiary of the company that holds the shares or its nominee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) the company that holds the shares or its nominee is a subsidiary of company A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) the company that holds the shares or its nominee is a subsidiary of a holding company of company A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held as treasury shares by company B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 594(5) the shares are disregarded` MEANS
    IF     `the shares are held by or by a nominee of company A`
        OR `s 1159(1) company A is a subsidiary of the company that holds the shares or its nominee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `s 1159(1) the company that holds the shares or its nominee is a subsidiary of company A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `s 1159(1) the company that holds the shares or its nominee is a subsidiary of a holding company of company A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `the shares are held as treasury shares by company B`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the following shall be disregarded— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..." names three kinds of shares

-- src:8030 | (2) This section applies to an arrangement for the allotment of shares in company A on terms that the whole or part of the consideration for the shares allotted is to be provided by—
-- src:8031 | (a) the transfer to that company, or
-- src:8032 | (b) the cancellation,
-- src:8033 | of all or some of the shares, or of all or some of the shares of a particular class, in another company (“company B”).
@ref s 594(2) the section applies to an arrangement for the allotment of shares in company A for shares in company B (src:8030-8033)
GIVEN `the arrangement is for the allotment of shares in company A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms are that the whole or part of the consideration is to be provided by the transfer to company A of all or some of the shares, or of all or some of the shares of a particular class, in company B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms are that the whole or part of the consideration is to be provided by the cancellation of all or some of the shares, or of all or some of the shares of a particular class, in company B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 594(2) the arrangement is of the kind to which section 594 applies` MEANS
    IF     `the arrangement is for the allotment of shares in company A`
       AND (    `the terms are that the whole or part of the consideration is to be provided by the transfer to company A of all or some of the shares, or of all or some of the shares of a particular class, in company B`
             OR `the terms are that the whole or part of the consideration is to be provided by the cancellation of all or some of the shares, or of all or some of the shares of a particular class, in company B`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to an arrangement for the allotment of shares in company A on terms that ... (a) the transfer ..., or (b) the cancellation"

-- src:8034 | (3) It is immaterial whether the arrangement provides for the issue to company A of shares, or shares of any particular class, in company B.
@ref s 594(3) it is immaterial whether the arrangement provides for the issue to company A of shares in company B (src:8034)
GIVEN `the arrangement provides for the issue to company A of shares, or shares of a particular class, in company B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 594(3) it matters to section 594 whether the arrangement provides for the issue to company A of shares in company B` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is immaterial whether the arrangement provides for the issue to company A of shares, or shares of any particular class, in company B"; the same answer whichever way the fact stands, so the input does not change it

-- src:8035 | (4) This section applies to an arrangement only if under the arrangement it is open to all the holders of the shares in company B (or, where the arrangement applies only to shares of a particular class, to all the holders of shares of that class) to take part in the arrangement.
@ref s 594(4) the section applies only if it is open to all the holders of the shares in company B to take part (src:8035)
GIVEN `s 594(2) the arrangement is of the kind to which section 594 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is open to all the holders of the shares in company B (or, where the arrangement applies only to shares of a particular class, to all the holders of shares of that class) to take part, disregarding the shares in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 594(4) the arrangement is one to which section 594 applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 594(2) the arrangement is of the kind to which section 594 applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `it is open to all the holders of the shares in company B (or, where the arrangement applies only to shares of a particular class, to all the holders of shares of that class) to take part, disregarding the shares in subsection (5)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to an arrangement only if under the arrangement it is open to all the holders of the shares in company B ... to take part"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) limits the application of the section and does not itself say which arrangements it applies to
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) does not decide the case

-- src:8029 | (1) Section 593 (valuation of non-cash consideration) does not apply to the allotment of shares by a company (“company A”) in connection with an arrangement to which this section applies.
@ref s 594(1) s 593 does not apply to the allotment of shares by company A in connection with an arrangement to which this section applies (src:8029)
GIVEN `s 594(4) the arrangement is one to which section 594 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 594(1) section 593 does not apply to the allotment` MEANS
    IF `s 594(4) the arrangement is one to which section 594 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to the allotment of shares by a company (“company A”) in connection with an arrangement to which this section applies"

-- src:8043 | (a) “arrangement” means any agreement, scheme or arrangement (including an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with—
-- src:8044 | (i) Part 26 or 26A (arrangements and reconstructions), or
-- src:8045 | (ii) section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)) (liquidator in winding up accepting shares as consideration for sale of company property)), and
@ref s 594(6)(a) "arrangement" means any agreement, scheme or arrangement, including one sanctioned under Part 26 or 26A or s 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (src:8043-8045)
GIVEN `it is an agreement, scheme or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part 26 and Part 26A it is an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26 or 26A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 594(6)(a) the thing is an arrangement` MEANS
    IF     `it is an agreement, scheme or arrangement`
        OR `Part 26 and Part 26A it is an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26 or 26A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `it is an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF     `Part 26 and Part 26A it is an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26 or 26A` EQUALS NOTHING
             OR `it is an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the thing is an arrangement sanctioned under Part 26, Part 26A or the Insolvency Act 1986 is not known
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“arrangement” means any agreement, scheme or arrangement (including an arrangement sanctioned in accordance with ...)"

-- src:8046 | (b) “company”, except in reference to company A, includes any body corporate.
@ref s 594(6)(b) "company", except in reference to company A, includes any body corporate (src:8046)
GIVEN `the reference is to company A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 594(6)(b) the body is a company for the purposes of section 594` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to company A`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): in reference to company A "company" keeps its ordinary meaning, which is section 1(1), not this subsection
    ELSE IF `the body is a body corporate`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“company”, except in reference to company A, includes any body corporate" does not close the list

-- ---- s 595: Exception to valuation requirement: merger or division ---------------------------------------

-- src:8048 | (1) Section 593 (valuation of non-cash consideration) does not apply to the allotment of shares by a company as part of a scheme to which Part 27 (mergers and divisions of public companies) applies if—
-- src:8049 | (a) in the case of a scheme involving a merger, an expert's report is drawn up as required by section 909, or
-- src:8050 | (b) in the case of a scheme involving a division, an expert's report is drawn up as required by section 924.
@ref s 595(1) s 593 does not apply to an allotment as part of a Part 27 scheme if the expert's report required by s 909 or s 924 is drawn up (src:8048-8050)
GIVEN `Part 27 the allotment is part of a scheme to which Part 27 (mergers and divisions of public companies) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the scheme involves a merger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 909 an expert's report is drawn up as required by section 909` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the scheme involves a division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 924 an expert's report is drawn up as required by section 924` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 595(1) section 593 does not apply to the allotment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Part 27 the allotment is part of a scheme to which Part 27 (mergers and divisions of public companies) applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF     (`the scheme involves a merger` AND `s 909 an expert's report is drawn up as required by section 909` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            OR (`the scheme involves a division` AND `s 924 an expert's report is drawn up as required by section 924` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE IF     (`the scheme involves a merger` AND `s 909 an expert's report is drawn up as required by section 909` EQUALS NOTHING)
                 OR (`the scheme involves a division` AND `s 924 an expert's report is drawn up as required by section 924` EQUALS NOTHING)
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the expert's report was drawn up as section 909 or 924 requires is not known
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply to the allotment of shares by a company as part of a scheme to which Part 27 applies if (a) ... an expert's report is drawn up as required by section 909, or (b) ... section 924" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as part of a scheme to which Part 27 (mergers and divisions of public companies) applies" (a condition that fails)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether Part 27 applies to the scheme is not known

-- ---- s 596: Non-cash consideration for shares: requirements as to valuation and report -----------------

-- src:8054 | (1) The provisions of sections 1150 to 1153 (general provisions as to independent valuation and report) apply to the valuation and report required by section 593 (public company: valuation of non-cash consideration for shares).
@ref s 596(1) ss 1150 to 1153 apply to the valuation and report required by s 593 (src:8054)
GIVEN `the valuation and report are required by section 593` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 596(1) sections 1150 to 1153 apply to the valuation and report` MEANS
    IF `the valuation and report are required by section 593`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to the valuation and report required by section 593"

-- src:8055 | (2) The valuer's report must state—
-- src:8056 | (a) the nominal value of the shares to be wholly or partly paid for by the consideration in question;
-- src:8057 | (b) the amount of any premium payable on the shares;
-- src:8058 | (c) the description of the consideration and, as respects so much of the consideration as he himself has valued, a description of that part of the consideration, the method used to value it and the date of the valuation;
-- src:8059 | (d) the extent to which the nominal value of the shares and any premium are to be treated as paid up—
-- src:8060 | (i) by the consideration;
-- src:8061 | (ii) in cash.
@ref s 596(2) the valuer's report must state the nominal value, the premium, the description of the consideration and the extent paid up (src:8055-8061)
GIVEN `the report states the nominal value of the shares to be wholly or partly paid for by the consideration in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the amount of any premium payable on the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the description of the consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the valuer himself has valued part of the consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report describes that part, the method used to value it and the date of the valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the extent to which the nominal value of the shares and any premium are to be treated as paid up by the consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the extent to which the nominal value of the shares and any premium are to be treated as paid up in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 596(2) the valuer's report meets the requirements as to what it must state` MEANS
    IF     `the report states the nominal value of the shares to be wholly or partly paid for by the consideration in question`
       AND `the report states the amount of any premium payable on the shares`
       AND `the report states the description of the consideration`
       AND ((NOT (`the valuer himself has valued part of the consideration`)) OR `the report describes that part, the method used to value it and the date of the valuation`)
       AND `the report states the extent to which the nominal value of the shares and any premium are to be treated as paid up by the consideration`
       AND `the report states the extent to which the nominal value of the shares and any premium are to be treated as paid up in cash`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The valuer's report must state— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... (d) ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:8062 | (3) The valuer's report must contain or be accompanied by a note by him—
-- src:8063 | (a) in the case of a valuation made by a person other than himself, that it appeared to himself reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made,
-- src:8064 | (b) whoever made the valuation, that the method of valuation was reasonable in all the circumstances,
-- src:8065 | (c) that it appears to the valuer that there has been no material change in the value of the consideration in question since the valuation, and
-- src:8066 | (d) that, on the basis of the valuation, the value of the consideration, together with any cash by which the nominal value of the shares or any premium payable on them is to be paid up, is not less than so much of the aggregate of the nominal value and the whole of any such premium as is treated as paid up by the consideration and any such cash.
@ref s 596(3) the valuer's report must contain or be accompanied by a note by the valuer (src:8062-8066)
GIVEN `the valuation was made by a person other than the valuer himself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note says that it appeared to the valuer reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note says that the method of valuation was reasonable in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note says that it appears to the valuer that there has been no material change in the value of the consideration since the valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note says that, on the basis of the valuation, the value of the consideration together with any cash is not less than so much of the aggregate of the nominal value and the premium as is treated as paid up by the consideration and the cash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 596(3) the valuer's report contains or is accompanied by the note required` MEANS
    IF     ((NOT (`the valuation was made by a person other than the valuer himself`)) OR `the note says that it appeared to the valuer reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made`)
       AND `the note says that the method of valuation was reasonable in all the circumstances`
       AND `the note says that it appears to the valuer that there has been no material change in the value of the consideration since the valuation`
       AND `the note says that, on the basis of the valuation, the value of the consideration together with any cash is not less than so much of the aggregate of the nominal value and the premium as is treated as paid up by the consideration and the cash`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The valuer's report must contain or be accompanied by a note by him— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... and (d) ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:8067 | (4) Where the consideration to be valued is accepted partly in payment up of the nominal value of the shares and any premium and partly for some other consideration given by the company, section 593 and the preceding provisions of this section apply as if references to the consideration accepted by the company included the proportion of that consideration that is properly attributable to the payment up of that value and any premium.
@ref s 596(4) where the consideration is accepted partly in payment up and partly for other consideration, the proportion attributable to payment up is valued (src:8067)
GIVEN `the consideration is accepted partly in payment up of the nominal value and any premium and partly for some other consideration given by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the consideration accepted by the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of that consideration that is properly attributable to the payment up of that value and any premium` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 596(4) the value of the consideration to be valued for the purposes of section 593 and section 596` MEANS
    IF `the consideration is accepted partly in payment up of the nominal value and any premium and partly for some other consideration given by the company`
    THEN `the value of the consideration accepted by the company` TIMES `the proportion of that consideration that is properly attributable to the payment up of that value and any premium`
    ELSE `the value of the consideration accepted by the company`

-- src:8068 | (5) In such a case—
-- src:8069 | (a) the valuer must carry out, or arrange for, such other valuations as will enable him to determine that proportion, and
-- src:8070 | (b) his report must state what valuations have been made under this subsection and also the reason for, and method and date of, any such valuation and any other matters which may be relevant to that determination.
@ref s 596(5) in such a case the valuer must carry out other valuations to determine the proportion, and his report must say what was done (src:8068-8070)
GIVEN `it is a case within subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the valuer carried out, or arranged for, such other valuations as will enable him to determine that proportion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `his report states what valuations have been made under the subsection, the reason for, and method and date of, any such valuation and any other matters which may be relevant to that determination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 596(5) the valuer and his report meet the requirements of subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF `it is a case within subsection (4)`
    THEN IF `the valuer carried out, or arranged for, such other valuations as will enable him to determine that proportion` AND `his report states what valuations have been made under the subsection, the reason for, and method and date of, any such valuation and any other matters which may be relevant to that determination`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the valuer must carry out, or arrange for, such other valuations ... and his report must state ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In such a case": the requirement is stated for a case within subsection (4) only (fork F-596(5))

-- ---- s 597: Copy of report to be delivered to registrar --------------------------------------------------

-- src:8072 | (1) A company to which a report is made under section 593 as to the value of any consideration for which, or partly for which, it proposes to allot shares must deliver a copy of the report to the registrar for registration.
@ref s 597(1) the company must deliver a copy of the valuer's report to the registrar for registration (src:8072)
GIVEN `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 597(1) the company has delivered the copy of the report to the registrar` MEANS
    `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery` -- JUST TRUE: delivered; JUST FALSE: not (yet) delivered properly; NOTHING (points outside the text) passes through

-- src:8073 | (2) The copy must be delivered at the same time that the company files the return of the allotment of those shares under section 555 (return of allotment by limited company).
@ref s 597(2) the copy must be delivered at the same time as the return of allotment under s 555 (src:8073)
GIVEN `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1071 the day the registrar received the document` IS A DATE
      `s 1071 the day the registrar received the return of allotment under section 555` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 597(2) the copy was delivered at the same time as the return of allotment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `s 1071 the day the registrar received the document` EQUALS `s 1071 the day the registrar received the return of allotment under section 555`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The copy must be delivered at the same time that the company files the return of the allotment" (taken as the same day: fork F-597(2))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The copy must be delivered" (a bare "must" not done)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1072 is not among the sources

-- src:8074 | (3) If default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 597(3) offence: if default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2), every officer in default (src:8074)
GIVEN `s 597(1) the company has delivered the copy of the report to the registrar` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 597(2) the copy was delivered at the same time as the return of allotment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 597(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `s 597(1) the company has delivered the copy of the report to the registrar` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 597(2) the copy was delivered at the same time as the return of allotment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 is not among the sources
    ELSE IF `s 597(1) the company has delivered the copy of the report to the registrar` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 597(2) the copy was delivered at the same time as the return of allotment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2)" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): default is not shown

-- src:8075 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:8076 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:8077 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of the statutory maximumone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences.
@ref s 597(4) penalty: on indictment a fine; on summary conviction a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum and a daily default fine (src:8075-8077)
`s 597(4)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- As in s 557(2)(b), the text shows two readings of the daily default fine run together and does not choose between them
-- (fork F-597(4)(b)), so the daily fine in the penalty is NOTHING and each reading has a function of its own, in pounds.
@ref s 597(4)(b) penalty on summary conviction (src:8077)
`s 597(4)(b) penalty on summary conviction` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text shows two readings and does not choose between them
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 597(4)(b) daily default fine, first reading: one-tenth of the statutory maximum (src:8077)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 597(4)(b) the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds, on the reading one-tenth of the statutory maximum` MEANS
    `the amount in pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` TIMES 0.1

@ref s 597(4)(b) daily default fine, second reading: one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount for level 4 (src:8077)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 4 on the standard scale stands for, for summary offences` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 597(4)(b) the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds, on the reading one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 and level 4` MEANS
    (max 5000 `the amount in pounds that level 4 on the standard scale stands for, for summary offences`) TIMES 0.1

@ref s 597(4) a person guilty of an offence under s 597 is liable (src:8075-8077)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 597(4) the penalties for an offence under section 597` MEANS
    LIST `s 597(4)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment`, `s 597(4)(b) penalty on summary conviction`

-- src:8078 | (5) In the case of default in delivering to the registrar any document as required by this section, any person liable for the default may apply to the court for relief.
@ref s 597(5) a person liable for the default may apply to the court for relief (src:8078)
GIVEN `the person is liable for the default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the default is in delivering to the registrar a document as required by section 597` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 597(5) the person may apply to the court for relief` MEANS
    IF `the person is liable for the default` AND `the default is in delivering to the registrar a document as required by section 597`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person liable for the default may apply to the court for relief" in the case of default in delivering a document as required by the section

-- src:8079 | (6) The court, if satisfied—
-- src:8080 | (a) that the omission to deliver the document was accidental or due to inadvertence, or
-- src:8081 | (b) that it is just and equitable to grant relief,
-- src:8082 | may make an order extending the time for delivery of the document for such period as the court thinks proper.
@ref s 597(6) the court, if satisfied, may extend the time for delivery (src:8079-8082)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the omission to deliver the document was accidental or due to inadvertence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 597(6) the court may make an order extending the time for delivery` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the omission to deliver the document was accidental or due to inadvertence` OR `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to grant relief`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court, if satisfied (a) ... or (b) ..., may make an order" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)

§§ `Transfer of non-cash asset in initial period (ss 598 to 604)`

-- ---- s 598: Public company: agreement for transfer of non-cash asset in initial period -----------------

-- src:8090 | (2) The company's “initial period” means the period of two years beginning with the date of the company being issued with a certificate under section 761 (trading certificate).
@ref s 598(2) the company's "initial period" is the period of two years beginning with the date of the s 761 certificate (src:8090)
GIVEN `s 761 the date on which the company is issued with a certificate under section 761 (trading certificate)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 598(2) the last day of the company's initial period` MEANS
    -- a period of two years beginning with the date includes that date, so it ends on the day before the second anniversary (fork F-598(2))
    (`add years` `s 761 the date on which the company is issued with a certificate under section 761 (trading certificate)` 2) MINUS 1

-- src:8094 | (4) This section does not apply where—
-- src:8095 | (a) it is part of the company's ordinary business to acquire, or arrange for other persons to acquire, assets of a particular description, and
-- src:8096 | (b) the agreement is entered into by the company in the ordinary course of that business.
@ref s 598(4) the section does not apply where the agreement is in the ordinary course of the company's business of acquiring assets (src:8094-8096)
GIVEN `it is part of the company's ordinary business to acquire, or arrange for other persons to acquire, assets of a particular description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is entered into by the company in the ordinary course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 598(4) section 598 does not apply to the agreement` MEANS
    IF `it is part of the company's ordinary business to acquire, or arrange for other persons to acquire, assets of a particular description` AND `the agreement is entered into by the company in the ordinary course of that business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply where (a) ... and (b) ..." (a "where" that fails)

-- src:8097 | (5) This section does not apply to an agreement entered into by the company under the supervision of the court or of an officer authorised by the court for the purpose.
@ref s 598(5) the section does not apply to an agreement entered into under the supervision of the court or an officer authorised by it (src:8097)
GIVEN `the agreement is entered into by the company under the supervision of the court or of an officer authorised by the court for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 598(5) section 598 does not apply to the agreement because of the court's supervision` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is entered into by the company under the supervision of the court or of an officer authorised by the court for the purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to an agreement entered into by the company under the supervision of the court or of an officer authorised by the court"

-- src:8085 | (1) A public company formed as such must not enter into an agreement—
-- src:8086 | (a) with a person who is a subscriber to the company's memorandum,
-- src:8087 | (b) for the transfer by him to the company, or another, before the end of the company's initial period of one or more non-cash assets, and
-- src:8088 | (c) under which the consideration for the transfer to be given by the company is at the time of the agreement equal in value to one-tenth or more of the company's issued share capital,
-- src:8089 | unless the conditions referred to below have been complied with.
@ref s 598(1) a public company formed as such must not enter into an agreement with a subscriber for the transfer of non-cash assets worth one-tenth or more of its issued share capital unless the conditions are complied with (src:8085-8089)
GIVEN `the company is a public company formed as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party is a person who is a subscriber to the company's memorandum (for a company re-registered as public: a person who is a member on the date of re-registration)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is for the transfer by him to the company, or another, of one or more non-cash assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date by which the transfer is to be made` IS A DATE
      `s 598(2) the last day of the company's initial period` IS A DATE
      `the value of the consideration for the transfer to be given by the company at the time of the agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the company's issued share capital` IS A NUMBER
      `s 598(4) section 598 does not apply to the agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 598(5) section 598 does not apply to the agreement because of the court's supervision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 599 the condition of independent valuation has been complied with` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 601 the condition of approval by members has been complied with` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 598(1) the public company is prohibited from entering into the agreement` MEANS
    IF     `the company is a public company formed as such`
       AND `the other party is a person who is a subscriber to the company's memorandum (for a company re-registered as public: a person who is a member on the date of re-registration)`
       AND `the agreement is for the transfer by him to the company, or another, of one or more non-cash assets`
       AND `the date by which the transfer is to be made` AT MOST `s 598(2) the last day of the company's initial period`
       AND `the value of the consideration for the transfer to be given by the company at the time of the agreement` AT LEAST (`the company's issued share capital` TIMES 0.1)
    THEN IF `s 598(4) section 598 does not apply to the agreement` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 598(5) section 598 does not apply to the agreement because of the court's supervision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply where ..." / "This section does not apply to an agreement entered into ... under the supervision of the court" (an exception is met)
         ELSE IF `s 599 the condition of independent valuation has been complied with` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 601 the condition of approval by members has been complied with` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not enter into an agreement ... unless the conditions referred to below have been complied with" (the "unless" is met)
              ELSE IF `s 599 the condition of independent valuation has been complied with` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 601 the condition of approval by members has been complied with` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company formed as such must not enter into an agreement— (a) with a person who is a subscriber ..., (b) for the transfer ... before the end of the company's initial period of one or more non-cash assets, and (c) under which the consideration ... is ... one-tenth or more of the company's issued share capital"

-- ---- s 599: Agreement for transfer of non-cash asset: requirement of independent valuation -----------------

-- src:8100 | (a) the consideration to be received by the company, and any consideration other than cash to be given by the company, must have been independently valued in accordance with the provisions of this Chapter,
@ref s 599(1)(a) the consideration to be received and any non-cash consideration to be given must have been independently valued (src:8100)
GIVEN `the consideration to be received by the company, and any consideration other than cash to be given by the company, has been independently valued in accordance with the provisions of Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 599(1)(a) the condition of independent valuation is met` MEANS
    IF `the consideration to be received by the company, and any consideration other than cash to be given by the company, has been independently valued in accordance with the provisions of Chapter 6`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following conditions must have been complied with— (a) ... must have been independently valued" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:8101 | (b) the valuer's report must have been made to the company during the six months immediately preceding the date of the agreement, and
@ref s 599(1)(b) the valuer's report must have been made to the company during the six months preceding the date of the agreement (src:8101)
GIVEN `the date on which the valuer's report was made to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date of the agreement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 599(1)(b) the condition that the report was made within the six months before the agreement is met` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the valuer's report was made to the company` AT MOST `the date of the agreement` AND `the date of the agreement` AT MOST (`add months` `the date on which the valuer's report was made to the company` 6)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the valuer's report must have been made to the company during the six months immediately preceding the date of the agreement" (a period fixed in its own words)

-- src:8102 | (c) a copy of the report must have been sent to the other party to the proposed agreement not later than the date on which copies have to be circulated to members under section 601(3).
@ref s 599(1)(c) a copy of the report must have been sent to the other party not later than the date on which copies have to be circulated to members under s 601(3) (src:8102)
GIVEN `the date on which a copy of the report was sent to the other party to the proposed agreement` IS A DATE
      `the date on which copies have to be circulated to members under section 601(3)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 599(1)(c) the condition that a copy was sent to the other party in time is met` MEANS
    -- Section 601(3) is shown blank in this text, so the date on which copies have to be circulated is an input (fork F-599(1)(c)).
    IF `the date on which a copy of the report was sent to the other party to the proposed agreement` AT MOST `the date on which copies have to be circulated to members under section 601(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) a copy of the report must have been sent to the other party to the proposed agreement not later than the date on which copies have to be circulated to members" (a bare "must" not done, and a time fixed in its own words)

-- src:8104 | (3) The reference in subsection (1)(c) to the other party to the proposed agreement is to the person referred to in section 598(1)(a).
-- src:8105 | If he has received a copy of the report under section 601 in his capacity as a member of the company, it is not necessary to send another copy under this section.
@ref s 599(3) a copy need not be sent again to the other party who has received one as a member under s 601 (src:8104-8105)
GIVEN `he has received a copy of the report under section 601 in his capacity as a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 599(3) it is necessary to send another copy under section 599` MEANS
    IF `he has received a copy of the report under section 601 in his capacity as a member of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary to send another copy under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a party who has received a copy under section 601 as a member

-- src:8099 | (1) The following conditions must have been complied with—
@ref s 599(1) the conditions of independent valuation must have been complied with (src:8099)
GIVEN `s 599(1)(a) the condition of independent valuation is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 599(1)(b) the condition that the report was made within the six months before the agreement is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 599(1)(c) the condition that a copy was sent to the other party in time is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 599(3) it is necessary to send another copy under section 599` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 599(1) the condition of independent valuation has been complied with` MEANS
    IF     `s 599(1)(a) the condition of independent valuation is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 599(1)(b) the condition that the report was made within the six months before the agreement is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `limb (c) is met or not needed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF     `s 599(1)(a) the condition of independent valuation is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
             OR `s 599(1)(b) the condition that the report was made within the six months before the agreement is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
             OR `limb (c) is met or not needed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following conditions must have been complied with— (a) ..., (b) ..., and (c) ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known
    WHERE
        -- the copy need not be sent to a party who has already received one as a member (subsection (3))
        `limb (c) is met or not needed` MEANS
            IF `s 599(3) it is necessary to send another copy under section 599` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE `s 599(1)(c) the condition that a copy was sent to the other party in time is met`

DECLARE `s 599(2) the consideration to be received by the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 599(2) the asset to be transferred to the company`
    `s 599(2) the advantage to the company of the asset's transfer to another person`

-- src:8103 | (2) The reference in subsection (1)(a) to the consideration to be received by the company is to the asset to be transferred to it or, as the case may be, to the advantage to the company of the asset's transfer to another person.
@ref s 599(2) the consideration to be received by the company is the asset, or the advantage of its transfer to another person (src:8103)
GIVEN `the asset is to be transferred to the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 599(2) the consideration to be received by the company`
`s 599(2) the consideration to be received by the company is` MEANS
    IF `the asset is to be transferred to the company itself`
    THEN `s 599(2) the asset to be transferred to the company`
    ELSE `s 599(2) the advantage to the company of the asset's transfer to another person`

-- src:8106 | (4) This section does not affect any requirement to value any consideration for purposes of section 593 (valuation of non-cash consideration for shares).
