GIVEN `there is a requirement to value consideration for the purposes of section 593` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 599(4) section 599 affects the requirement to value consideration for the purposes of section 593` MEANS
    IF `there is a requirement to value consideration for the purposes of section 593`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect any requirement to value any consideration for purposes of section 593"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a requirement to value for the purposes of section 593

-- ---- s 600: Agreement for transfer of non-cash asset: requirements as to valuation and report ------------

-- src:8108 | (1) The provisions of sections 1150 to 1153 (general provisions as to independent valuation and report) apply to the valuation and report required by section 599 (public company: transfer of non-cash asset).
@ref s 600(1) ss 1150 to 1153 apply to the valuation and report required by s 599 (src:8108)
GIVEN `the valuation and report are required by section 599` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
