    IF `the valuation and report are required by section 599`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to the valuation and report required by section 599"

-- src:8109 | (2) The valuer's report must state—
-- src:8110 | (a) the consideration to be received by the company, describing the asset in question (specifying the amount to be received in cash) and the consideration to be given by the company (specifying the amount to be given in cash), and
-- src:8111 | (b) the method and date of valuation.
@ref s 600(2) the valuer's report must state the consideration to be received and given, with the cash amounts, and the method and date of valuation (src:8109-8111)
GIVEN `the report states the consideration to be received by the company, describing the asset in question and specifying the amount to be received in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the consideration to be given by the company, specifying the amount to be given in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the method and date of valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 600(2) the valuer's report meets the requirements as to what it must state` MEANS
    IF     `the report states the consideration to be received by the company, describing the asset in question and specifying the amount to be received in cash`
       AND `the report states the consideration to be given by the company, specifying the amount to be given in cash`
       AND `the report states the method and date of valuation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The valuer's report must state— (a) ... and (b) the method and date of valuation" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:8112 | (3) The valuer's report must contain or be accompanied by a note by him—
-- src:8113 | (a) in the case of a valuation made by a person other than himself, that it appeared to himself reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made,
-- src:8114 | (b) whoever made the valuation, that the method of valuation was reasonable in all the circumstances,
-- src:8115 | (c) that it appears to the valuer that there has been no material change in the value of the consideration in question since the valuation, and
-- src:8116 | (d) that, on the basis of the valuation, the value of the consideration to be received by the company is not less than the value of the consideration to be given by it.
@ref s 600(3) the valuer's report must contain or be accompanied by a note by the valuer (src:8112-8116)
GIVEN `the valuation was made by a person other than the valuer himself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note says that it appeared to the valuer reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note says that the method of valuation was reasonable in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note says that it appears to the valuer that there has been no material change in the value of the consideration since the valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the note says that, on the basis of the valuation, the value of the consideration to be received by the company is not less than the value of the consideration to be given by it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 600(3) the valuer's report contains or is accompanied by the note required` MEANS
    IF     ((NOT (`the valuation was made by a person other than the valuer himself`)) OR `the note says that it appeared to the valuer reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made`)
       AND `the note says that the method of valuation was reasonable in all the circumstances`
       AND `the note says that it appears to the valuer that there has been no material change in the value of the consideration since the valuation`
       AND `the note says that, on the basis of the valuation, the value of the consideration to be received by the company is not less than the value of the consideration to be given by it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The valuer's report must contain or be accompanied by a note by him— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... and (d) ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:8117 | (4) Any reference in section 599 or this section to consideration given for the transfer of an asset includes consideration given partly for its transfer.
@ref s 600(4) consideration given for the transfer of an asset includes consideration given partly for its transfer (src:8117)
GIVEN `the consideration is given partly for the transfer of the asset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 600(4) the consideration is consideration given for the transfer of the asset for the purposes of sections 599 and 600` MEANS
    IF `the consideration is given partly for the transfer of the asset`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes consideration given partly for its transfer" does not close the list

-- src:8118 | (5) In such a case—
-- src:8119 | (a) the value of any consideration partly so given is to be taken as the proportion of the consideration properly attributable to its transfer,
-- src:8120 | (b) the valuer must carry out or arrange for such valuations of anything else as will enable him to determine that proportion, and
-- src:8121 | (c) his report must state what valuations have been made for that purpose and also the reason for and method and date of any such valuation and any other matters which may be relevant to that determination.
@ref s 600(5) in such a case the proportion attributable to the transfer is valued and the report states what valuations were made (src:8118-8121)
GIVEN `the consideration is given partly for the transfer of the asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the consideration given` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of the consideration properly attributable to its transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 600(5)(a) the value of the consideration partly so given, taken as the proportion attributable to the transfer` MEANS
    IF `the consideration is given partly for the transfer of the asset`
    THEN `the value of the consideration given` TIMES `the proportion of the consideration properly attributable to its transfer`
    ELSE `the value of the consideration given`

@ref s 600(5)(b) and (c) the valuer must carry out other valuations to determine the proportion, and his report must state what was done (src:8119-8121)
GIVEN `it is a case within subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the valuer carried out, or arranged for, such valuations of anything else as will enable him to determine that proportion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `his report states what valuations have been made for that purpose, the reason for and method and date of any such valuation and any other matters which may be relevant to that determination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 600(5)(b) the valuer and his report meet the requirements of subsection (5)(b) and (c)` MEANS
    IF `it is a case within subsection (4)`
    THEN IF `the valuer carried out, or arranged for, such valuations of anything else as will enable him to determine that proportion` AND `his report states what valuations have been made for that purpose, the reason for and method and date of any such valuation and any other matters which may be relevant to that determination`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the valuer must carry out or arrange for such valuations ... and (c) his report must state ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In such a case": the requirement is stated for a case within subsection (4) only (fork F-596(5))

-- ---- s 601: Agreement for transfer of non-cash asset: requirement of approval by members -----------------

-- src:8124 | (a) the terms of the agreement must have been approved by an ordinary resolution of the company,
@ref s 601(1)(a) the terms of the agreement must have been approved by an ordinary resolution of the company (src:8124)
GIVEN `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution approves the terms of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 601(1)(a) the condition of approval by ordinary resolution is met` MEANS
    IF `the resolution approves the terms of the agreement`
    THEN `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` -- JUST TRUE: met; JUST FALSE: a bare "must" not done (a fork line); NOTHING passes through
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the terms of the agreement must have been approved by an ordinary resolution of the company" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:8125 | (b) copies of the valuer's report must have been circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting at which the resolution is proposed, not later than the date on which notice of the meeting is given, and
@ref s 601(1)(b) copies of the valuer's report must have been circulated to the members entitled to notice not later than the date on which notice is given (src:8125)
GIVEN `the date on which copies of the valuer's report were circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting at which the resolution is proposed` IS A DATE
      `the date on which notice of the meeting is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 601(1)(b) the condition that the report was circulated in time is met` MEANS
    IF `the date on which copies of the valuer's report were circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting at which the resolution is proposed` AT MOST `the date on which notice of the meeting is given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "copies of the valuer's report must have been circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting ... not later than the date on which notice of the meeting is given" (a bare "must" not done, and a time fixed in its own words)

-- src:8126 | (c) a copy of the proposed resolution must have been sent to the other party to the proposed agreement.
@ref s 601(1)(c) a copy of the proposed resolution must have been sent to the other party (src:8126)
GIVEN `a copy of the proposed resolution has been sent to the other party to the proposed agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 601(1)(c) the condition that a copy of the proposed resolution was sent to the other party is met` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the proposed resolution has been sent to the other party to the proposed agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a copy of the proposed resolution must have been sent to the other party to the proposed agreement" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:8123 | (1) The following conditions must have been complied with—
@ref s 601(1) the conditions of approval by members must have been complied with (src:8123)
GIVEN `s 601(1)(a) the condition of approval by ordinary resolution is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 601(1)(b) the condition that the report was circulated in time is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 601(1)(c) the condition that a copy of the proposed resolution was sent to the other party is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 601(1) the condition of approval by members has been complied with` MEANS
    IF     `s 601(1)(a) the condition of approval by ordinary resolution is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 601(1)(b) the condition that the report was circulated in time is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 601(1)(c) the condition that a copy of the proposed resolution was sent to the other party is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF     `s 601(1)(a) the condition of approval by ordinary resolution is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
             OR `s 601(1)(b) the condition that the report was circulated in time is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
             OR `s 601(1)(c) the condition that a copy of the proposed resolution was sent to the other party is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following conditions must have been complied with— (a) ..., (b) ..., and (c) ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known

-- src:8127 | (2) The reference in subsection (1)(c) to the other party to the proposed agreement is to the person referred to in section 598(1)(a).
@ref s 601(2) the other party in subsection (1)(c) is the person referred to in s 598(1)(a) (src:8127)
GIVEN `the person is the person referred to in section 598(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
