GIVEN `the person is the person referred to in section 598(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 599(3) the person is the other party to the proposed agreement for the purposes of subsection (1)(c)` MEANS
    IF `the person is the person referred to in section 598(1)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reference in subsection (1)(c) to the other party to the proposed agreement is to the person referred to in section 598(1)(a)"

-- ---- s 602: Copy of resolution to be delivered to registrar ----------------------------------------------

-- src:8130 | (1) A company that has passed a resolution under section 601 with respect to the transfer of an asset must, within 15 days of doing so, deliver to the registrar a copy of the resolution together with the valuer's report required by that section.
@ref s 602(1) a company that has passed a resolution under s 601 must within 15 days deliver a copy with the valuer's report (src:8130)
GIVEN `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1071 the day the registrar received the document` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company passed the resolution` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 602(1) the company has delivered the copy of the resolution and the valuer's report in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `s 1071 the day the registrar received the document` AT MOST `the last day for delivering the copy`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 15 days of doing so" (a period fixed in its own words; delivery was after it)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the last day for delivering the copy`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 15 days of doing so" (the 15 days have ended and nothing proper has been delivered)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 15 days have not ended, so the text does not yet say the company has failed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1072 is not among the sources
    WHERE
        `the last day for delivering the copy` MEANS `the date on which the company passed the resolution` PLUS 15

-- src:8131 | (2) If a company fails to comply with subsection (1), an offence is committed by—
-- src:8132 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8133 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 602(2) offence: if a company fails to comply, the company and every officer in default (src:8131-8133)
GIVEN `s 602(1) the company has delivered the copy of the resolution and the valuer's report in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 602(2)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 602(1) the company has delivered the copy of the resolution and the valuer's report in time`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (1), an offence is committed" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the company has not yet failed to comply

@ref s 602(2)(b) offence by every officer of the company who is in default (src:8133)
GIVEN `s 602(1) the company has delivered the copy of the resolution and the valuer's report in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 602(2)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 602(1) the company has delivered the copy of the resolution and the valuer's report in time`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 is not among the sources
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (1), an offence is committed" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the company has not yet failed to comply

-- src:8134 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, to a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 602(3) penalty: summary conviction, level 3, and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 3 (src:8134)
`s 602(3) penalty on summary conviction` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 602(3) the most the fine can be, in pounds (src:8134)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 602(3) the most the fine can be, in pounds` MEANS `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`

@ref s 602(3) the daily default fine, in pounds (src:8134)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 602(3) the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds` MEANS `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` TIMES 0.1

-- ---- s 603: Adaptation of provisions in relation to company re-registering as public -------------------

-- src:8136 | The provisions of sections 598 to 602 (public companies: transfer of non-cash assets) apply with the following adaptations in relation to a company re-registered as a public company—
-- src:8137 | (a) the reference in section 598(1)(a) to a person who is a subscriber to the company's memorandum shall be read as a reference to a person who is a member of the company on the date of re-registration;
