`s 603(a) the person is within the reference in section 598(1)(a) for a company re-registered as a public company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the company on the date of re-registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the reference in section 598(1)(a) to a person who is a subscriber to the company's memorandum shall be read as a reference to a person who is a member of the company on the date of re-registration"

-- src:8138 | (b) the reference in section 598(2) to the date of the company being issued with a certificate under section 761 (trading certificate) shall be read as a reference to the date of re-registration.
