    `the date of re-registration`

-- ---- s 604: Agreement for transfer of non-cash asset: effect of contravention ---------------------------

-- src:8140 | (1) This section applies where a public company enters into an agreement in contravention of section 598 and either—
-- src:8141 | (a) the other party to the agreement has not received the valuer's report required to be sent to him, or
-- src:8142 | (b) there has been some other contravention of the requirements of this Chapter that the other party to the agreement knew or ought to have known amounted to a contravention.
@ref s 604(1) the section applies where a public company enters into an agreement in contravention of s 598 and the other party has not received the report or knew of another contravention (src:8140-8142)
GIVEN `a public company enters into an agreement in contravention of section 598` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party to the agreement has not received the valuer's report required to be sent to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been some other contravention of the requirements of Chapter 6 that the other party to the agreement knew or ought to have known amounted to a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 604(1) section 604 applies` MEANS
    IF     `a public company enters into an agreement in contravention of section 598`
       AND (`the other party to the agreement has not received the valuer's report required to be sent to him` OR `there has been some other contravention of the requirements of Chapter 6 that the other party to the agreement knew or ought to have known amounted to a contravention`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a public company enters into an agreement in contravention of section 598 and either (a) ... or (b) ..." (a "where" that fails)

-- src:8143 | (2) In those circumstances—
-- src:8144 | (a) the company is entitled to recover from that person any consideration given by it under the agreement, or an amount equal to the value of the consideration at the time of the agreement, and
@ref s 604(2)(a) the company is entitled to recover the consideration given, or its value at the time of the agreement (src:8143-8144)
GIVEN `s 604(1) section 604 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 604(2)(a) the company is entitled to recover from that person the consideration it gave, or its value` MEANS
    `s 604(1) section 604 applies` -- JUST TRUE: "In those circumstances" are met; JUST FALSE: a "where" that fails; NOTHING passes through

-- src:8145 | (b) the agreement, so far as not carried out, is void.
@ref s 604(2)(b) the agreement, so far as not carried out, is void (src:8145)
GIVEN `s 604(1) section 604 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 604(2)(b) the agreement, so far as not carried out, is void` MEANS
    `s 604(1) section 604 applies` -- JUST TRUE: "In those circumstances" are met; JUST FALSE: a "where" that fails; NOTHING passes through

-- src:8146 | (3) If the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company, then—
-- src:8147 | (a) whether or not the agreement also contravenes section 593 (valuation of non-cash consideration for shares), this section does not apply to it in so far as it is for the allotment of shares, and
@ref s 604(3)(a) for an agreement that includes the allotment of shares, section 604 does not apply in so far as it is for the allotment (src:8146-8147)
GIVEN `the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 604(3)(a) section 604 does not apply to the agreement in so far as it is for the allotment of shares` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company"

-- src:8146 | (3) If the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company, then—
-- src:8147 | (a) whether or not the agreement also contravenes section 593 (valuation of non-cash consideration for shares), this section does not apply to it in so far as it is for the allotment of shares, and
-- src:8148 | (b) the allottee is liable to pay the company an amount equal to the aggregate of the nominal value of the shares and the whole of any premium (or, if the case so requires, so much of that aggregate as is treated as paid up by the consideration), with interest at the appropriate rate.
@ref s 604(3)(b) the allottee is liable to pay the company the nominal value and the whole of any premium, with interest (src:8146-8148)
GIVEN `the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 604(3)(b) the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company, then ... (b) the allottee is liable" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

@ref s 604(3)(b) the amount: the nominal value and the whole premium, or so much as is treated as paid up by the consideration (src:8148)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole of any premium on them` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up by the consideration (1 if the whole)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 604(3)(b) the amount the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    (`the nominal value of the shares` PLUS `the whole of any premium on them`) TIMES `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up by the consideration (1 if the whole)`

§§ `Supplementary provisions (ss 605 to 609)`

-- ---- s 605: Liability of subsequent holders of shares ----------------------------------------------------

-- src:8161 | (3) A person otherwise liable under subsection (1) or (2) is exempted from that liability if either—
-- src:8162 | (a) he is a purchaser for value and, at the time of the purchase, he did not have actual notice of the contravention concerned, or
-- src:8163 | (b) he derived title to the shares (directly or indirectly) from a person who became a holder of them after the contravention and was not liable under subsection (1) or (2).
@ref s 605(3) a person otherwise liable is exempted if a purchaser for value without actual notice, or if he derived title from a person not liable (src:8161-8163)
GIVEN `he is a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the purchase he did not have actual notice of the contravention concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he derived title to the shares (directly or indirectly) from a person who became a holder of them after the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person was not liable under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 605(3) the person is exempted from the liability` MEANS
    IF     (`he is a purchaser for value` AND `at the time of the purchase he did not have actual notice of the contravention concerned`)
        OR (`he derived title to the shares (directly or indirectly) from a person who became a holder of them after the contravention` AND `that person was not liable under subsection (1) or (2)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is exempted from that liability if either (a) ... or (b) ..." (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

-- src:8151 | (1) If a person becomes a holder of shares in respect of which—
-- src:8152 | (a) there has been a contravention of section 593 (public company: valuation of non-cash consideration for shares), and
-- src:8153 | (b) by virtue of that contravention another is liable to pay any amount under the provision contravened,
-- src:8154 | that person is also liable to pay that amount (jointly and severally with any other person so liable), unless he is exempted from liability under subsection (3) below.
@ref s 605(1) a person who becomes a holder of shares in respect of which a contravention of s 593 makes another liable is also liable, unless exempted (src:8151-8154)
GIVEN `there has been a contravention of section 593 in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by virtue of that contravention another is liable to pay an amount under the provision contravened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 605(3) the person is exempted from the liability` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 605(1) the person who becomes a holder is also liable to pay the amount` MEANS
    IF `there has been a contravention of section 593 in respect of the shares` AND `by virtue of that contravention another is liable to pay an amount under the provision contravened`
    THEN IF `s 605(3) the person is exempted from the liability` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he is exempted from liability under subsection (3) below" (the "unless" is met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE -- an exemption that answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING is read as not met (fork F-588)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person becomes a holder of shares in respect of which (a) there has been a contravention of section 593 ..., and (b) by virtue of that contravention another is liable" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

-- src:8155 | (2) If a company enters into an agreement in contravention of section 598 (public company: agreement for transfer of non-cash asset in initial period) and—
-- src:8156 | (a) the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company,
-- src:8157 | (b) a person becomes a holder of shares allotted under the agreement, and
-- src:8158 | (c) by virtue of the agreement and allotment under it another person is liable to pay an amount under section 604,
-- src:8159 | the person who becomes the holder of the shares is also liable to pay that amount (jointly and severally with any other person so liable), unless he is exempted from liability under subsection (3) below.
-- src:8160 | This applies whether or not the agreement also contravenes section 593.
@ref s 605(2) a person who becomes a holder of shares allotted under an agreement that contravenes s 598 is also liable for the amount payable under s 604, unless exempted (src:8155-8160)
GIVEN `a company enters into an agreement in contravention of section 598` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person becomes a holder of shares allotted under the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by virtue of the agreement and allotment under it another person is liable to pay an amount under section 604` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 605(3) the person is exempted from the liability` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 605(2) the person who becomes the holder of the shares is also liable to pay the amount` MEANS
    IF     `a company enters into an agreement in contravention of section 598`
       AND `the agreement is or includes an agreement for the allotment of shares in the company`
       AND `the person becomes a holder of shares allotted under the agreement`
       AND `by virtue of the agreement and allotment under it another person is liable to pay an amount under section 604`
    THEN IF `s 605(3) the person is exempted from the liability` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he is exempted from liability under subsection (3) below" (the "unless" is met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE -- an exemption that answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING is read as not met (fork F-588)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company enters into an agreement in contravention of section 598 (public company: agreement for transfer of non-cash asset in initial period) and— (a) ... (b) ... and (c) ..." (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

-- src:8164 | (4) References in this section to a holder, in relation to shares in a company, include any person who has an unconditional right—
-- src:8165 | (a) to be included in the company's register of members ... in respect of those shares, or
-- src:8166 | (b) to have an instrument of transfer of the shares executed in his favour.
@ref s 605(4) the holder includes a person with an unconditional right to be on the register of members or to have an instrument of transfer executed (src:8164-8166)
GIVEN `the person has an unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has an unconditional right to have an instrument of transfer of the shares executed in his favour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 605(4) the person is within the reference to a holder of shares` MEANS
    IF `the person has an unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares` OR `the person has an unconditional right to have an instrument of transfer of the shares executed in his favour`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include any person who has an unconditional right" does not close the list

-- ---- s 606: Power of court to grant relief ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:8168 | (1) A person who—
-- src:8169 | (a) is liable to a company under any provision of this Chapter in relation to payment in respect of any shares in the company, or
-- src:8170 | (b) is liable to a company by virtue of an undertaking given to it in, or in connection with, payment for any shares in the company,
-- src:8171 | may apply to the court to be exempted in whole or in part from the liability.
@ref s 606(1) a person liable under the Chapter in relation to payment, or by virtue of an undertaking, may apply to the court to be exempted (src:8168-8171)
GIVEN `the person is liable to a company under a provision of Chapter 6 in relation to payment in respect of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is liable to a company by virtue of an undertaking given to it in, or in connection with, payment for shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(1) the person may apply to the court to be exempted from the liability in whole or in part` MEANS
    IF `the person is liable to a company under a provision of Chapter 6 in relation to payment in respect of shares in the company` OR `the person is liable to a company by virtue of an undertaking given to it in, or in connection with, payment for shares in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who (a) is liable to a company under any provision of this Chapter ... or (b) is liable to a company by virtue of an undertaking ... may apply to the court"

-- src:8172 | (2) In the case of a liability within subsection (1)(a), the court may exempt the applicant from the liability only if and to the extent that it appears to the court just and equitable to do so having regard to—
-- src:8173 | (a) whether the applicant has paid, or is liable to pay, any amount in respect of—
-- src:8174 | (i) any other liability arising in relation to those shares under any provision of this Chapter or Chapter 5, or
-- src:8175 | (ii) any liability arising by virtue of any undertaking given in or in connection with payment for those shares;
-- src:8176 | (b) whether any person other than the applicant has paid or is likely to pay, whether in pursuance of any order of the court or otherwise, any such amount;
-- src:8177 | (c) whether the applicant or any other person—
-- src:8178 | (i) has performed in whole or in part, or is likely so to perform any such undertaking, or
-- src:8179 | (ii) has done or is likely to do any other thing in payment or part payment for the shares.
@ref s 606(2) in the case of a liability within subsection (1)(a), the court may exempt the applicant only if and to the extent that it appears just and equitable (src:8172-8179)
GIVEN `it appears to the court just and equitable to exempt the applicant, having regard to whether the applicant has paid or is liable to pay any amount in respect of any other liability or undertaking, whether any other person has paid or is likely to pay any such amount, and whether the applicant or any other person has performed or is likely to perform any such undertaking or done any other thing in payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(2) the court may exempt the applicant from a liability within subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the court just and equitable to exempt the applicant, having regard to whether the applicant has paid or is liable to pay any amount in respect of any other liability or undertaking, whether any other person has paid or is likely to pay any such amount, and whether the applicant or any other person has performed or is likely to perform any such undertaking or done any other thing in payment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may exempt the applicant from the liability only if and to the extent that it appears to the court just and equitable to do so" (the judgment of the court is a plain input)

-- src:8180 | (3) In the case of a liability within subsection (1)(b), the court may exempt the applicant from the liability only if and to the extent that it appears to the court just and equitable to do so having regard to—
-- src:8181 | (a) whether the applicant has paid or is liable to pay any amount in respect of liability arising in relation to the shares under any provision of this Chapter or Chapter 5;
-- src:8182 | (b) whether any person other than the applicant has paid or is likely to pay, whether in pursuance of any order of the court or otherwise, any such amount.
@ref s 606(3) in the case of a liability within subsection (1)(b), the court may exempt the applicant only if and to the extent that it appears just and equitable (src:8180-8182)
GIVEN `it appears to the court just and equitable to exempt the applicant, having regard to whether the applicant has paid or is liable to pay any amount in respect of liability arising in relation to the shares under Chapter 5 or Chapter 6, and whether any other person has paid or is likely to pay any such amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(3) the court may exempt the applicant from a liability within subsection (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the court just and equitable to exempt the applicant, having regard to whether the applicant has paid or is liable to pay any amount in respect of liability arising in relation to the shares under Chapter 5 or Chapter 6, and whether any other person has paid or is likely to pay any such amount`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may exempt the applicant from the liability only if and to the extent that it appears to the court just and equitable to do so" (the judgment of the court is a plain input)

-- src:8183 | (4) In determining whether it should exempt the applicant in whole or in part from any liability, the court must have regard to the following overriding principles—
-- src:8184 | (a) that a company that has allotted shares should receive money or money's worth at least equal in value to the aggregate of the nominal value of those shares and the whole of any premium or, if the case so requires, so much of that aggregate as is treated as paid up;
@ref s 606(4)(a) overriding principle: the company should receive money or money's worth at least equal to the nominal value and premium (src:8183-8184)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole of any premium on them` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up (1 if the whole)` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the money or money's worth the company would receive if the exemption were granted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(4)(a) the principle that the company should receive at least the aggregate is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the value of the money or money's worth the company would receive if the exemption were granted` AT LEAST ((`the nominal value of the shares` PLUS `the whole of any premium on them`) TIMES `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up (1 if the whole)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that a company that has allotted shares should receive money or money's worth at least equal in value to the aggregate of the nominal value of those shares and the whole of any premium" (the principle is not satisfied)

-- src:8185 | (b) subject to this, that where such a company would, if the court did not grant the exemption, have more than one remedy against a particular person, it should be for the company to decide which remedy it should remain entitled to pursue.
@ref s 606(4)(b) subject to this, where the company has more than one remedy it is for the company to decide which to pursue (src:8185)
GIVEN `the company would, if the court did not grant the exemption, have more than one remedy against a particular person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 606(4)(a) the principle that the company should receive at least the aggregate is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(4)(b) it is for the company to decide which remedy it should remain entitled to pursue` MEANS
    IF `the company would, if the court did not grant the exemption, have more than one remedy against a particular person`
    THEN IF `s 606(4)(a) the principle that the company should receive at least the aggregate is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to this": the first principle prevails and the text does not say what follows when it is not satisfied
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where such a company would, if the court did not grant the exemption, have more than one remedy against a particular person"

-- src:8186 | (5) If a person brings proceedings against another (“the contributor”) for a contribution in respect of liability to a company arising under any provision of this Chapter or Chapter 5 and it appears to the court that the contributor is liable to make such a contribution, the court may, if and to the extent that it appears to it, just and equitable to do so having regard to the respective culpability (in respect of the liability to the company) of the contributor and the person bringing the proceedings—
-- src:8187 | (a) exempt the contributor in whole or in part from his liability to make such a contribution, or
-- src:8188 | (b) order the contributor to make a larger contribution than, but for this subsection, he would be liable to make.
@ref s 606(5) in contribution proceedings the court may exempt the contributor or order a larger contribution (src:8186-8188)
GIVEN `a person brings proceedings against another (“the contributor”) for a contribution in respect of liability to a company arising under any provision of Chapter 5 or Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the contributor is liable to make such a contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court just and equitable to do so, having regard to the respective culpability (in respect of the liability to the company) of the contributor and the person bringing the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(5) the court may exempt the contributor in whole or in part, or order a larger contribution` MEANS
    IF     `a person brings proceedings against another (“the contributor”) for a contribution in respect of liability to a company arising under any provision of Chapter 5 or Chapter 6`
       AND `it appears to the court that the contributor is liable to make such a contribution`
    THEN IF `it appears to the court just and equitable to do so, having regard to the respective culpability (in respect of the liability to the company) of the contributor and the person bringing the proceedings`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may, if and to the extent that it appears to it, just and equitable to do so having regard to the respective culpability" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person brings proceedings against another (“the contributor”) for a contribution ... and it appears to the court that the contributor is liable to make such a contribution"

-- src:8189 | (6) Where a person is liable to a company under section 604(2) (agreement for transfer of non-cash asset: effect of contravention), the court may, on application, exempt him in whole or in part from that liability if and to the extent that it appears to the court to be just and equitable to do so having regard to any benefit accruing to the company by virtue of anything done by him towards the carrying out of the agreement mentioned in that subsection.
@ref s 606(6) where a person is liable under s 604(2), the court may exempt him having regard to any benefit accruing to the company (src:8189)
GIVEN `the person is liable to a company under section 604(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court to be just and equitable to exempt him, having regard to any benefit accruing to the company by virtue of anything done by him towards the carrying out of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(6) the court may exempt the person from the liability under section 604(2)` MEANS
    IF `the person is liable to a company under section 604(2)`
    THEN IF `it appears to the court to be just and equitable to exempt him, having regard to any benefit accruing to the company by virtue of anything done by him towards the carrying out of the agreement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may, on application, exempt him in whole or in part from that liability if and to the extent that it appears to the court to be just and equitable" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is liable to a company under section 604(2)" (a "where" that fails)

-- ---- s 607: Penalty for contravention of this Chapter ----------------------------------------------------

-- src:8191 | (1) This section applies where a company contravenes—
-- src:8192 | section 593 (public company allotting shares for non-cash consideration), or
-- src:8193 | section 598 (public company entering into agreement for transfer of non-cash asset).
@ref s 607(1) the section applies where a company contravenes s 593 or s 598 (src:8191-8193)
GIVEN `the company contravenes section 593 (public company allotting shares for non-cash consideration) or section 598 (public company entering into agreement for transfer of non-cash asset)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 607(1) section 607 applies` MEANS
    IF `the company contravenes section 593 (public company allotting shares for non-cash consideration) or section 598 (public company entering into agreement for transfer of non-cash asset)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company contravenes— section 593 ..., or section 598 ..." (a "where" that fails)

-- src:8194 | (2) An offence is committed by—
-- src:8195 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8196 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 607(2) offence by the company and every officer of the company who is in default (src:8194-8196)
GIVEN `s 607(1) section 607 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 607(2)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    `s 607(1) section 607 applies` -- JUST TRUE: an offence is committed by the company; JUST FALSE: the "where" of subsection (1) fails; NOTHING passes through

@ref s 607(2)(b) offence by every officer of the company who is in default (src:8196)
GIVEN `s 607(1) section 607 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 607(2)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 607(1) section 607 applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 is not among the sources
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company contravenes" (a "where" that fails)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 607 applies is not known

-- src:8197 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:8198 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:8199 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 607(3) penalty: on indictment a fine; on summary conviction a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (src:8197-8199)
`s 607(3)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 607(3)(b) penalty on summary conviction (src:8199)
`s 607(3)(b) penalty on summary conviction` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 607(3) a person guilty of an offence under s 607 is liable (src:8197-8199)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 607(3) the penalties for an offence under section 607` MEANS
    LIST `s 607(3)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment`, `s 607(3)(b) penalty on summary conviction`

-- ---- s 608: Enforceability of undertakings to do work etc ------------------------------------------------

-- src:8201 | (1) An undertaking given by any person, in or in connection with payment for shares in a company, to do work or perform services or to do any other thing, if it is enforceable by the company apart from this Chapter, is so enforceable notwithstanding that there has been a contravention in relation to it of a provision of this Chapter or Chapter 5.
@ref s 608(1) an undertaking enforceable by the company apart from the Chapter remains enforceable despite a contravention (src:8201)
GIVEN `the undertaking is given by a person, in or in connection with payment for shares in a company, to do work or perform services or to do any other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is enforceable by the company apart from Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 608(1) the undertaking is enforceable by the company despite a contravention of Chapter 6 or Chapter 5` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is given by a person, in or in connection with payment for shares in a company, to do work or perform services or to do any other thing`
    THEN IF `it is enforceable by the company apart from Chapter 6`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is enforceable by the company apart from this Chapter, is so enforceable" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An undertaking given by any person, in or in connection with payment for shares in a company, to do work or perform services or to do any other thing"

-- src:8202 | (2) This is without prejudice to section 606 (power of court to grant relief etc in respect of liabilities).
@ref s 608(2) this is without prejudice to s 606 (src:8202)
GIVEN `the matter is the court's power under section 606 to grant relief in respect of liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 608(2) section 608(1) prejudices the court's power under section 606` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the court's power under section 606 to grant relief in respect of liabilities`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is without prejudice to section 606"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of section 606 only

-- ---- s 609: The appropriate rate of interest -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:8204 | (1) For the purposes of this Chapter the “appropriate rate” of interest is 5% per annum or such other rate as may be specified by order made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 609(1) the appropriate rate of interest is 5% per annum or such other rate as may be specified by order (src:8204)
GIVEN `the other rate specified by an order made by the Secretary of State under section 609(1), as a fraction per annum, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 609(1) the appropriate rate of interest, as a fraction per annum` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the other rate specified by an order made by the Secretary of State under section 609(1), as a fraction per annum, if there is one`
    WHEN JUST rate THEN rate
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0.05
